cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it as below. A paper describing it is
  under submission; this entry will be updated on publication.
title: >-
  KernelCert: a Lean reference for Certifaiger's hardware model-checking certificate
  checks, a reference checker compiled from it, and a conformance study
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ghonim
    given-names: Mohamed
    affiliation: Portland State University
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8311-059X
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Xiaoyu
    affiliation: Portland State University
repository-code: https://github.com/Ghonimo/kernelcert-conformance
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - hardware model checking
  - certificates
  - witness circuits
  - Certifaiger
  - Lean 4
  - differential testing
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof that Certifaiger's safety checks imply safety (constraints, reset
  functions that read inputs and latches, uninitialized latches, and the reset side
  condition of Certifaiger 10.3.0), including that Certifaiger's own Transition formula
  implies the mechanized one; a reference checker (kcheck) whose acceptances are proved to
  imply safety, for circuits small enough to enumerate; and a pre-registered conformance study comparing it with Certifaiger,
  Valaig and an explicit-state ground truth.
